{
    "id": "grammar-1",
    "title": "Ser vs Estar",
    "type": "grammar",
    "description": "Understanding when to use 'ser' and 'estar' - two verbs that both mean 'to be'",
    "description_fr": "Comprendre quand utiliser 'ser' et 'estar' - deux verbes qui signifient 'être'",
    "content": {
        "intro": {
            "en": "Spanish has TWO verbs for 'to be': **SER** and **ESTAR**. This confuses many learners, but there's a simple rule!",
            "fr": "L'espagnol a DEUX verbes pour 'être' : **SER** et **ESTAR**. Cela déroute beaucoup d'apprenants, mais il y a une règle simple !"
        },
        "sections": [
            {
                "title": {
                    "en": "SER - Permanent Characteristics",
                    "fr": "SER - Caractéristiques permanentes"
                },
                "explanation": {
                    "en": "Use **SER** for things that don't change easily: identity, nationality, profession, physical traits, time, and relationships.",
                    "fr": "Utilisez **SER** pour les choses qui ne changent pas facilement : identité, nationalité, profession, traits physiques, heure et relations."
                },
                "examples": [
                    {
                        "spanish": "Yo soy María.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "I am María.",
                            "fr": "Je suis María."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "spanish": "Él es doctor.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "He is a doctor.",
                            "fr": "Il est médecin."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "spanish": "Somos de España.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "We are from Spain.",
                            "fr": "Nous sommes d'Espagne."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "spanish": "Son las tres.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "It's three o'clock.",
                            "fr": "Il est trois heures."
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": {
                    "en": "🔒 SER = Stable/Permanent (DOCTOR = Description, Occupation, Characteristic, Time, Origin, Relationship)",
                    "fr": "🔒 SER = Stable/Permanent (DOCTOR = Description, Occupation, Caractéristique, Temps, Origine, Relation)"
                }
            },
            {
                "title": {
                    "en": "ESTAR - Temporary States & Locations",
                    "fr": "ESTAR - États temporaires & Lieux"
                },
                "explanation": {
                    "en": "Use **ESTAR** for things that can change: feelings, moods, locations, and temporary conditions.",
                    "fr": "Utilisez **ESTAR** pour les choses qui peuvent changer : sentiments, humeurs, lieux et conditions temporaires."
                },
                "examples": [
                    {
                        "spanish": "Estoy cansado.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "I am tired.",
                            "fr": "Je suis fatigué."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "spanish": "Ella está en casa.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "She is at home.",
                            "fr": "Elle est à la maison."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "spanish": "Estamos contentos.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "We are happy.",
                            "fr": "Nous sommes contents."
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "spanish": "La puerta está abierta.",
                        "translation": {
                            "en": "The door is open.",
                            "fr": "La porte est ouverte."
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "mnemonic": {
                    "en": "📍 ESTAR = Emotions, States, Temporary conditions, Actions in progress, and Locations (ESTAL)",
                    "fr": "📍 ESTAR = Émotions, États, Temporaire, Actions en cours, et Lieux (ESTAL)"
                }
            },
            {
                "title": {
                    "en": "Conjugation Chart",
                    "fr": "Tableau de conjugaison"
                },
                "table": {
                    "headers": [
                        "Pronoun",
                        "SER",
                        "ESTAR"
                    ],
                    "rows": [
                        [
                            "yo",
                            "soy",
                            "estoy"
                        ],
                        [
                            "tú",
                            "eres",
                            "estás"
                        ],
                        [
                            "él/ella/usted",
                            "es",
                            "está"
                        ],
                        [
                            "nosotros",
                            "somos",
                            "estamos"
                        ],
                        [
                            "ellos/ustedes",
                            "son",
                            "están"
                        ]
                    ]
                }
            }
        ],
        "tip": {
            "en": "💡 Some adjectives change meaning! 'Ser aburrido' = to be boring (personality), but 'Estar aburrido' = to be bored (feeling).",
            "fr": "💡 Certains adjectifs changent de sens ! 'Ser aburrido' = être ennuyeux (personnalité), mais 'Estar aburrido' = s'ennuyer (sentiment)."
        }
    },
